---
title: Package version phases and helper instance states (implemented)
---
stateDiagram-v2
  direction LR
  state "Package version (VersionPhase)" as Version {
    [*] --> Staged : install or update verified and published, approvals or waits recorded
    Staged --> Installed : approval recorded, no waits left, activated at the next quiescent boundary
    Staged --> Staged : retry_pending, wait is Quiescence or Compatibility only
    Staged --> Rejected : person rejects it in decide_proposal
    Staged --> Removed : newer proposal or uninstall retires the candidate
    Installed --> Installed : rollback target or reinstall, no new approval needed
    Installed --> Removed : uninstall then collect_files after helper retirement
    Rejected --> [*] : install or propose of the same digest is refused with Conflict
    Removed --> Staged : same contents proposed or installed again, unapproved, files republished
    Removed --> Installed : proposed again but approved earlier
  }
  state "Helper instance (InstanceStatus)" as Instance {
    [*] --> Starting : reconcile finds enabled, installed, available package
    Starting --> Ready : host.initialize then host.activate handshake echoes digest and revisions
    Starting --> HelperFailed : handshake or launch failure, restart with backoff
    Ready --> Retiring : registry changed (new digest, generation or configuration)
    Ready --> HelperFailed : helper exits, in-flight invocations end OutcomeUnknown
    HelperFailed --> Starting : restart up to restart_limit
    Retiring --> Stopped : in-flight invocations finished or cancelled
    Ready --> Stopped : disable, uninstall or shutdown cancels invocations then stops the tree
    HelperFailed --> Stopped : limit reached, failure recorded, guarded automatic rollback if nothing ran
  }
  note right of Version
    Waits that block Staged: ExactVersionApproval, TrustApproval, AccessApproval,
    Compatibility, Quiescence. A person's own install or update approves the exact digest.
    Agent-authored or proposed contents always need a person.
  end note
  note right of Instance
    invoke is admitted only on a Ready instance of the active version with no barrier up.
    The helper is a separate process, not an OS sandbox.
  end note
